    "result_text": "All 32 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn successful owner creation, the endpoint now emits an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger containing the owner id, customerCode, and registrationDate.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** (new function class) \u2014 logs to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n\n   public void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n       AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n               owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a new `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs after the owner is persisted (id assigned) and stays inside the transaction governance like the surrounding steps:\n   ```yaml\n   save:\n     ...\n     next: audit\n   audit:\n     class: ...owner.AuditOwnerCreated\n     govern: [ transaction ]\n     next: respond\n   ```\n\nThis follows the project's OfficeFloor conventions (one public method per step, state passed via `@Val Owner`, placed after `save` so the id is present). The `Cp21Tests` audit-create test and the full suite (32 tests) pass green.",
